Lets the core keep Chrome's warning before http out of an agent's tab (//browser_core/hooks.h,
//browser_core/secure_connections.h). The warning is a dialog whose Continue to site loads the
page over http and remembers the site: the user's to press. Where Chrome would show it, the tab
helper asks the core first; the core answers for the tab the page is in and, in an agent's, puts
the tab back itself, so no warning ever exists there. The helper holds no rule of its own.

--- a/chrome/browser/ssl/https_only_mode_tab_helper.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ssl/https_only_mode_tab_helper.cc
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 // found in the LICENSE file.
 
